20260521 - 
• The app is not failing on type. It is reading a database file whose provenance table is currently empty.

  What I verified against /Users/mduby/Code/PythonWorkspace/GeneSetExtractor/python-flask-server/data/genseco_v0.sqlite:

  - SELECT COUNT(*) FROM provenance; returns 0
  - SELECT ... FROM provenance WHERE gene_set_id = 1; returns no rows
  - the Python helper returns None for both provenance fields
  - the app resolves DB_PATH to that same file

  I also checked for SQLite WAL sidecars:

  - no genseco_v0.sqlite-wal
  - no genseco_v0.sqlite-shm
  - PRAGMA journal_mode; returns delete

  So the likely explanations are:

  - you ran the query against a different genseco_v0.sqlite
  - you have a different copy open elsewhere
  - the row existed in an uncommitted session and is not in this file now

  If you want, I can make the service expose the exact DB path in a health/debug endpoint so there’s no ambiguity, or add startup logging of the resolved SQLite file.


